  "description": "Term-count profile of the Bokut-Shiao corner's a <= b chain. The two quadratic steps each add one term (peak 4); exactly TWO later steps remove two at once, which no rewrite can do -- each is a pair of terms reconverging on one word with opposite coefficients and annihilating. The first is mid-prefix; the second IS the final step, so reaching zero is itself a cancellation rather than a separate terminating mechanism. The assembly needs a CoeffEq bridging lemma for this, used twice -- not just MultiStepReduction.trans.",
